{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_50","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json, os\nfor d in ['/workspace/run_trace/galaxy_tool_schema_004','/workspace/run_trace/galaxy_tool_schema_003']:\n    p=os.path.join(d,'build_response.json')\n    if os.path.exists(p):\n        x=json.load(open(p))\n        print('\\\\n===',d,'===')\n        print(x.get('help','')[:5000])\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"\n=== /workspace/run_trace/galaxy_tool_schema_004 ===\n<p>KEGG ORA performs pathway over-representation analysis from a foreground gene\nlist and a pathway mapping. It reports one row per pathway with foreground\nhits, pathway size, universe size, hypergeometric upper-tail p-value, and\nBenjamini-Hochberg adjusted p-value.</p>\n<p>Use a supplied or pinned mapping table for reproducible analyses, fixed database\nsnapshots, or organisms/databases that are not directly supported by an\ninstalled Galaxy enrichment wrapper. KEGG REST mode can download a current KEGG\norganism mapping when network access is available to the Galaxy job.</p>\n<p>The p-value adjustment family can be all pathways with at least one gene in the\nuniverse, or only pathways with at least one foreground hit. The summary output\nrecords the mapping source, mapping hash, background mode, adjustment family,\nuniverse size, foreground size, and pathway counts used in the run.</p>\n<p>The contributing-genes output has one row per foreground gene that maps to a\npathway and is useful for counting which genes contribute to a selected pathway.</p>\n\n\n=== /workspace/run_trace/galaxy_tool_schema_003 ===\n<p>This tool converts common rectangular R objects stored in <cite>.rds</cite>, <cite>.rdata</cite>, or\n<cite>.rda</cite> files into Galaxy tabular datasets. Auto-detection uses known filename\nextensions when available and falls back to trying both RDS and RData readers\nfor extensionless Galaxy dataset paths.</p>\n<p>Use this for analysis results saved as a single R object, for example a\ndifferential-expression result table. It is intentionally different from older\n<cite>.RData</cite> extraction tools that call <cite>load()</cite> and cannot read <cite>.rds</cite> files.</p>\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
