{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_130","type":"agent_message","text":"The standard clusterProfiler-style ORA adjusts across pathways that actually have foreground hits, not zero-hit pathways. Under that definition, the three-strain intersection is two down-regulated pathways and none up-regulated. I’m also checking whether the background choice changes that conclusion."}}
